# Daily Work Operator — Product Rules

## What this is

A local-first personal work app for a single product designer/developer. When
the user starts work, the app tells them:

1. What to do first
2. Why it matters
3. What the next concrete action is
4. How they know it is truly done

## What this is NOT

- Not a full project management app. No sprint planning, no team assignment,
  no multi-user workflows, no Gantt/roadmap views.
- Do not add features that belong to Jira/Linear/Asana-style PM tools (backlog
  grooming, story points, burndown charts, team dashboards).
- If a proposed feature could be summarized as "manage a team's work," it is
  out of scope. This app manages one person's next move.

## Data sources (eventual)

Manual transcripts, Granola transcripts, Gmail / Gemini / Google Meet notes,
Jira, Confluence, GitHub, Figma, Discord, local git repositories. Treat these
as read-only signal sources that feed task generation, not systems the app
manages.

## Core task model

Every task the app surfaces (AI-generated or manual) must carry:

- **Evidence** — the source snippet/link/quote that justifies the task
  existing (transcript line, Jira ticket, PR, email, etc.)
- **Next action** — a single concrete, immediately doable step
- **Done criteria** — an explicit, checkable definition of "truly done"

Never create or render a task missing any of these three fields.

## Unclear bucket

If ownership (who owns this) or the requirement itself is ambiguous, do not
guess or force it into a normal task. Route it to an explicit **Unclear**
bucket/state where it's flagged for the user to resolve manually.
